"answer": "Project Zenith was initiated in Q3 2023 under leader Marcus Cole to optimize cloud storage solutions. The project involved gathering R&D ideas by July 20th, securing a $2M budget, and forming a strategic partnership with TechInnovate. Initial findings suggested a 20% efficiency increase via AI algorithms. The team expanded with new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing. The project progressed through design and development phases, led by Omar Jensen, and successfully completed its testing phase. A celebration was scheduled for October 10th. However, a final email from Dan announced that Project Zenith has been cancelled."
